      "title": "Santner wary of Sooryavanshi, expects Bhuvneshwar to enjoy NZ conditions",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/cricket/news/santner-wary-of-sooryavanshi-expects-bhuvneshwar-to-enjoy-nz-conditions-126102100336_1.html",
      "description": "New Zealand captain Mitchell Santner conceded that Vaibhav Sooryavanshi would be \"quite hard to stop\" if he plays for India in the five-match T20 International series beginning here on Thursday, but his team has some plans to deal with the young batting sensation.\nSooryavanshi has been used sparingly since being picked for the tour of UK earlier this year, largely because regular openers Abhishek Sharma and Sanju Samson have done the job quite well. Santner said should the 15-year-old make the playing XI in the series here, some research has been done to figure out his game.\n\"He (Sooryavanshi) did not play in the last series (against West Indies), but we know how good he is, in IPL. We know other players like Abhishek are doing very well. But he (Sooryavanshi) has a huge part to play for India, whether it's in this series or not, but in future,\" Santner said at the pre-series press conference here on Wednesday.\n\"If he does get a crack at this series, we've seen what he can do and gu",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-21T10:41:16"
    },
    {
      "title": "Iyer backs Sanju and Abhishek as openers, says Sooryavanshi must wait",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/cricket/news/iyer-backs-sanju-and-abhishek-as-openers-says-sooryavanshi-must-wait-126102100189_1.html",
      "description": "India T20 captain Shreyas Iyer on Wednesday said young batting sensation Vaibhav Sooryavanshi cannot \"walk\" into the playing eleven just yet as Abhishek Sharma and Sanju Samson are scoring consistently at the top, insisting that the teenager will get his chances in due course.\nSince being picked for the England and Ireland tour earlier this year, Sooryavanshi has featured in eight of the 21 T20Is India have played so far as regular openers Abhishek and Samson have been performing consistently.\nBoth of them played a key role in India defending their T20I World Cup title earlier this year.\n\"It's important that a talent like him (Sooryavanshi) should always be happy around the dressing room,\" Iyer said on the eve of a five-match series against New Zealand here.\n\"He is very young, he has more years to get opportunities. It's not like he can walk in right now, because our openers are scoring consistently, and they have won the World Cup.\"\nAt the Asian Games, Samson dropped down to numb",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-21T04:57:09"
    }
